       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in MS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " gait problems may be treated w ER 4-aminopyridine (dalfampridine)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dalfampridine ER (Ampyra) dose, walking in multiple sclerosis:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 10 mg ER tablet PO BID, ~12 h apart; do ⍉exceed. ⍉added benefit >10 mg BID; adverse rxns incl sz more freq @ higher doses. Take w or w/o food; administer tablets whole — do ⍉divide, crush, chew, or dissolve. Missed dose: do ⍉take double or extra doses. Estimate CrCl b4 initiating and monitor at least annually during tx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dalfampridine ER (Ampyra) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Hx of sz. CI: mod or severe renal impairment (CrCl≤50 mL/min). CI: Hx of hypersensitivity to AMPYRA or 4-aminopyridine (incl anaphylaxis)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dalfampridine ER (Ampyra) warnings:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Sz: permanently d/c and do ⍉restart if a sz occurs on tx. Mild renal impairment (CrCl 51–80 mL/min): plasma levels may approach those @ 15 mg BID, ↑ sz risk — weigh benefit vs risk. ⍉ concomitant other forms of 4-aminopyridine (4-AP, fampridine) — same active ingredient. Anaphylaxis/severe allergic rxns: resp compromise, urticaria, angioedema of throat/tongue; instruct pts to d/c and seek immediate medical care if these occur."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
